# Android builds

- This Mac has a dedicated Android toolchain. Before any Node, Android, or Gradle build command, run `source ~/android-toolchain/env.sh`.
- That environment provides Node.js 22, JDK 21, `ANDROID_HOME`, `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT`, SDK tools, and `adb`.
- For MoneyLit AABs, inspect this project's release signing first, then run the native Gradle `bundleRelease` task. This is React Native/Expo, not Capacitor; do not run `npx cap sync`.
- Do not start an EAS build unless the user explicitly asks for EAS for that build.
- Expected AAB output: `android/app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab`.
- Never reuse another app's package name or keystore.
- Before triggering any remote build, state which build system will be used and obtain confirmation if the user did not already name it.
